-- Source module: Solutions.KFMTabQ
/-!
# KFM 9d: the `d`-axis chirp array — outer products of the axis tables

`chirpArr Δ d s t` is the row-major array (last axis innermost) of the chirp entries
`chirpEnt Δ s t j`, built by `d` outer products `oprod Δ A B = [Q_Δ(a b) | a ∈ A, b ∈ B]`
starting from `[1]`:

* **`chirpArr_get`**: entry `flatIx j` of `chirpArr` is `chirpEnt Δ s t j` (the `Q_Δ`-product of
  the `d` axis-table factors, `KFMTabM`);
* **`chirpArr_err`**: it is within `d (8T² + 2) 2^{-Δ}` of `RC.chirp s t j`;
* **`chirpArr_near`**: every entry is within that distance of a point of the unit disc, so all
  entries have `Δ + 2`-bit components (`NearU.bnd`).

The IL program is `chirpP` (below), one level `levP` per axis: `axG` (axis table), then for each
entry `a` of the current array a replicate / copy / `gmulP` / move-out round (`obB`).
-/

